---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import examples from '../data/client-examples.json';
import { publicCurl } from '../data/public-query';
import { gradleDependencies, SEMPODS_VERSION, SEMPODS_RELEASE_URL, implementationDoc, specificationDoc } from '../data/coordinates';
const sourceUrl = implementationDoc(examples.source.path);
---

<Base
  title="Start with sempods — build a client, implement the contract or run a pod"
  description="Query a public pod, use the Kotlin 0.2 JVM client, implement the open contract, or run the development composition. Choose the path that fits your task."
  schemaType="TechArticle"
>
  <p class="eyebrow">try it yourself</p>
  <h1>Start with a real pod. Then choose your path.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Read three events from a public pod. No account or installation needed.
    Then build a client, read the contract, or run a pod yourself.
  </p>

  <section id="query" class="try-block">
    <h2>Query and follow the data</h2>
    <pre><code>{publicCurl}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The response contains <code>e</code>, <code>name</code> and <code>start</code>.
      Open one of the event URIs in <code>e</code> to read its JSON-LD description.
      The venue keeps the data; your client can use it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href="#build">Build an app</a>{' '}
    <a href="#implement">Implement the contract</a>{' '}
    <a href="#run">Run a pod</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="build">Build against a pod</h2>
  <p>
    Use HTTP and JSON-LD directly, or start with the JVM client. The{' '}<a href={SEMPODS_RELEASE_URL}>Kotlin {SEMPODS_VERSION} release</a> is on Maven Central.
    Select one BOM version for the modules you use:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{gradleDependencies}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>sempods-client</code>: HTTP, JSON-LD text, bytes, SPARQL results and OAuth helpers; Java 21+.</li>
    <li><code>sempods-client-rdf4j</code>: RDF4J models and values; Java 25+.</li>
    <li><code>sempods-client-media</code>: binary media operations; Java 21+.</li>
    <li><code>sempods-control-plane-client</code>: host administration; Java 21+.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Read a public resource</h3>
  <p>
    Set <code>podUrl</code> to the full pod URL and <code>resourceIri</code> to
    a resource in that pod. The snippets use <code>org.sempods.client.*</code>{' '}and <code>okhttp3.OkHttpClient</code>. Install the client policy once:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{examples.snippets.install}</code></pre>
  <p>Bind a session and read the resource. Check the status before using the body:</p>
  <pre><code>{examples.snippets.publicRead}</code></pre>
  <p class="evidence">
    These snippets come from the <a href={sourceUrl}>tested release source</a>.
    The complete test supplies the imports and a local HTTP fixture.
  </p>
  <p>
    For private data, choose <a href={implementationDoc('sempods-server/docs/auth/user-access.md')}>delegated access</a>{' '}when acting for a person, or <a href={implementationDoc('sempods-server/docs/auth/service-clients.md')}>service access</a>{' '}for a backend acting as itself. Service registration and owner consent are
    experimental Kotlin 0.2 extensions.
  </p>
  <p>
    Coming from 0.1? The client API changed, and RDF4J and media moved into
    separate adapters. Read the <a href={implementationDoc('docs/migration/0.2.md')}>migration guide</a>{' '}before raising the BOM.
  </p>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href={implementationDoc('sempods-client/README.md')}>JVM client guide</a>{' '}
    <a href="/concepts/mcp-over-pods">Connect an agent</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="implement">Implement the open contract</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://spec.sempods.org">development specification</a> defines
    the public contract: authorized RDF access, HTTP CRUD, SPARQL and retrieval,
    with optional modules such as MCP and media. It can be implemented in a
    different language or on a different store.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose a complete specification revision. Core and modules version
    independently of each other and of Kotlin. A <code>0.1-dev</code> label
    needs its source commit to identify what you implemented.
  </p>
  <p>
    The normative text already determines the contract. Proposals describe
    possible changes; they do not change the requirements. A product conformance
    suite remains unfinished, so document known deviations.
  </p>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href="https://spec.sempods.org/api/">Explore the HTTP surface</a>{' '}
    <a href={specificationDoc('docs/guides/specification-revisions.md')}>Select a revision</a>{' '}
    <a href={specificationDoc('GOVERNANCE.md')}>Read governance</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="run">Compose or run a pod</h2>
  <p>
    sempods-kotlin supplies reusable services and libraries. A deployment chooses
    their implementations and configuration. Start with the release's{' '}<a href={implementationDoc('README.md#quick-start')}>local quick start</a>{' '}to run the development composition with Java 25 and Docker Compose.
  </p>
  <p>
    That composition supports development and evaluation. A concrete deployment
    owns backups, version transitions and recovery; the supplied stack has no
    supported upgrade path. Read <a href={implementationDoc('docs/concepts/modularity.md#deployment-and-upgrades')}>deployment responsibilities</a>{' '}before using it for persistent data.
  </p>
  <p>
    AI routes are disabled unless a provider is configured. Media and identity
    also depend on your chosen composition. The release guides explain the
    settings rather than assuming every service is needed.
  </p>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href={implementationDoc('README.md#the-three-services')}>Choose services</a>{' '}
    <a href={implementationDoc('docs/concepts/modularity.md')}>Explore the building blocks</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="explore">Explore before operating anything</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://apps.sempods.org/explorer/">Explorer</a> is an experimental
    graph browser. Point it at a public pod to see resources and links together.
    A preview app's availability is separate from the Kotlin release.
  </p>
  <figure class="media-breakout">
    <a href="/images/explorer-aaltra.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open larger Explorer screenshot">
      <img src="/images/explorer-aaltra.webp" width="1600" height="1005" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
        alt="Explorer displaying a linked event graph from the aaltra pod" />
    </a>
    <figcaption>One event, its dates and its links, read from the aaltra pod.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>
    Need a test pod or a starting point for your own setup?{' '}<a href="mailto:hello@sempods.org">Write to hello@sempods.org</a>.
    Hosting is arranged manually; there is no public hosting dashboard.
  </p>
  <p class="action-links">
    <a href="/links">Find project resources</a>{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/sempods/sempods-kotlin/issues">Report an implementation problem</a>
  </p>
</Base>
